  <bpmn:collaboration id="L4_02_COLLAB" name="Identify protocol deviations">
    <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Model: L4-02
Title: Identify protocol deviations
Parent: L3 A2
Interface: start S1; ends E1, E2; message flows M1
Rule exception: ROL-03 P_INV - D1 (orchestrator default, 06 Nov 2026): Investigator/institution is an expanded pool on all levels because investigator obligations are binding steps that must appear as tasks
Rule exception: DEC-06 G3 - XOR split G3: each branch is a distinct business outcome (E1, E2) and ends in its own end event without a join
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring process 'Data governance and computerised systems' configures the audit trails and metadata that A2 reviews; set-up process without a flow hand-off, so no placeholder element. Interface REQs: REQ-209.
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring process 'Safety reporting' (SAE to sponsor, EU CTR Art. 41(2), 24 h) runs in parallel when a deviation causes an SAE; the investigator OR split already has 3 branches (FLW-06). Interface REQs: REQ-214.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:participant id="L4_02_P_SPON" name="Sponsor" processRef="L4_02_P_SPON_PROCESS">
      <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Sources: E6R3 GL:Sponsor (p. printed 90 / PDF 98); EUCTR Art. 47 (p. OJ L 158/39); 21CFR312 21CFR312.50 (p. n/a - eCFR web text without pagination); E6R3 P3.1 (p. printed 4 / PDF 12); E6R3 A1-3.9.2 (p. printed 26 / PDF 34); E6R3 P10.1 (p. printed 7 / PDF 15); E6R3 P10.3 (p. printed 7 / PDF 15); E6R3 A1-3.9.5 (p. printed 27 / PDF 35); E6R3 A2-3.8 (p. printed 62 / PDF 70); EMA-SB SGlossary (p. printed 3/21); TCB-RBQM SQTL-Process (p. journal pp. 251-261 (section page not confirmed))</bpmn:documentation>
