    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:inclusiveGateway id="L4_02_G1" name="Which monitoring channels are due?" gatewayDirection="Diverging" default="L4_02_F2">
      <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Justification: Centralised monitoring can complement and reduce site monitoring or be used on its own (E6R3 A1-3.11.4.2(b)) and site visit frequency follows the risks (A1-3.11.4.1(a)), so one or both channels run in a cycle (FLW-07, DEC-02). Centralised data review is the default flow because quality control applies at each stage of data handling (A1-3.11.3). XOR rejected: the channels are not exclusive.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>L4_02_F1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>L4_02_F2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>L4_02_F3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:inclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="L4_02_A1" name="Review trial data for protocol deviations">
      <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Sources: E6R3 A1-3.11.4.5.4(b)(ii) (p. printed 34 / PDF 42); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.2(a) (p. printed 31 / PDF 39); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.2(b) (p. printed 31 / PDF 39); E8R1 S6.1.3 (p. printed 18); E8R1 S3.3.2 (p. printed 6); E6R3 A1-3.11.3 (p. printed 30 / PDF 38); E6R3 A1-3.16.1(b) (p. printed 39 / PDF 47); E6R3 A2-3.8 (p. printed 62 / PDF 70); E6R3 A1-3.11.4.5.4(c) (p. printed 34 / PDF 42); FDA-RBM13 SIII.B (p. printed 8); FDA-PD24 SIII.B.2 (p. printed 6; lines 227-228; printed 9; lines 314-317); TCB-PD-TIRS SIdentify-and-Collect (p. journal pp. 733-742 (section page not confirmed; PMC HTML read))
