  <bpmn:collaboration id="L4_05_COLLAB" name="Assess and notify reportable noncompliance">
    <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Model: L4-05
Title: Assess and notify reportable noncompliance
Parent: L3 A5
Interface: start S1; ends E1, E2; message flows M1, M2, M3
Rule exception: ROL-03 P_INV - D1 (orchestrator default, 06 Nov 2026): Investigator/institution is an expanded pool on all levels because investigator obligations are binding steps that must appear as tasks
Rule exception: DEC-06 G9 - XOR split G9: each branch is a distinct business outcome (E1, E2) and ends in its own end event without a join
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring process 'Data security incident handling': an incident that is also serious noncompliance or a serious breach enters this step through S1. Interface REQs: REQ-212.
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring process 'IND safety reporting and unanticipated problems' (21 CFR 312.32, 312.55, 312.66, 56.108(b)(1)): runs when a deviation reveals or contributes to a reportable safety event; no flow hand-off is defined in the sources. Interface REQs: REQ-224, REQ-225, REQ-227, REQ-228, REQ-229.
Open item: [verify interface] IRB/IEC-internal process 'Suspension or termination of IRB approval' inside the collapsed IRB/IEC pool (D1); its reports are not part of this step. Interface REQs: REQ-230.
Open item: [verify interface] Authority-initiated processes after a notification (CTIS request for information; corrective measures, EU CTR Art. 77): each starts with an incoming authority request, so it is a separate process (SCP-02). The authority's assessment of the notification (REQ-231) is attached to message flow M1. Interface REQs: REQ-232, REQ-233, REQ-234.</bpmn:documentation>
