  <bpmn:collaboration id="L4_06_COLLAB" name="Remediate deviations and noncompliance">
    <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">Model: L4-06
Title: Remediate deviations and noncompliance
Parent: L3 A6
Interface: start S1; ends E1, E2; message flows M1, M5
Rule exception: ROL-03 P_INV - D1 (orchestrator default, 06 Nov 2026): Investigator/institution is an expanded pool on all levels because investigator obligations are binding steps that must appear as tasks
Rule exception: DEC-06 G6 - XOR split G6: branch 'Yes' is the distinct business outcome E2 (investigator participation terminated) and ends without rejoining G9
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring process 'Quality assurance and audit': its findings enter L4-04/L4-05 as potential deviations or noncompliance and its CAPA requests enter this step. Interface REQs: REQ-208.
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring process 'Protocol amendment (21 CFR 312.30; EU CTR Chapter III)' runs when an amendment is the corrective action; the sources define no decision point inside this step. Interface REQs: REQ-221, REQ-222.
Open item: [verify interface] Neighbouring processes 'Restart after temporary halt (EU CTR)' and 'Discontinuation for unreasonable risk (21 CFR 312.56(d))' are safety and trial status processes. Interface REQs: REQ-223, REQ-226.</bpmn:documentation>
